From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stuart Marks <swmarks@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 12:51:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libcec: fallback to Power On Function if Image View On is
 unsupported

Some displays (e.g. Hisense) successfully wake upon receiving an initial
Image View On (0x04) command, but subsequently send a Feature Abort for
it. libCEC caches this abort, causing subsequent wake attempts to skip
Image View On and only send Active Source, leaving the display asleep.

This patch adds a fallback to CCECCommandHandler::PowerOn. If the target
is the TV and Image View On is marked as unsupported, it falls back to
transmitting User Control Pressed: Power On Function (0x6D). This reliably
wakes the display on subsequent attempts without requiring us to bypass
the opcode cache or maintain vendor-specific blocklists.

Reported-by: rama1313 (Discord)

LibreELEC Hades: taken unchanged from pannal/CoreELEC commit
9e288911577f5cd38e433dd36bdb8456b784409b
(libcec-003-fallback-power-on-function.patch). In libcec 8.1.7 a command
whose opcode the destination aborted once is not sent again, and
CCECCommandHandler::Transmit() reports it as sent.
---
 src/libcec/implementations/CECCommandHandler.cpp | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/libcec/implementations/CECCommandHandler.cpp b/src/libcec/implementations/CECCommandHandler.cpp
index ac05daf..a8e01b1 100644
--- a/src/libcec/implementations/CECCommandHandler.cpp
+++ b/src/libcec/implementations/CECCommandHandler.cpp
@@ -943,7 +943,16 @@ void CCECCommandHandler::SetPhysicalAddress(cec_logical_address iAddress, uint16
 bool CCECCommandHandler::PowerOn(const cec_logical_address iInitiator, const cec_logical_address iDestination)
 {
   if (iDestination == CECDEVICE_TV)
+  {
+    CCECBusDevice* tv = m_processor->GetDevice(iDestination);
+    if (tv && tv->IsUnsupportedFeature(CEC_OPCODE_IMAGE_VIEW_ON))
+    {
+      return TransmitKeypress(iInitiator, iDestination, CEC_USER_CONTROL_CODE_POWER_ON_FUNCTION) &&
+        TransmitKeyRelease(iInitiator, iDestination);
+    }
+
     return TransmitImageViewOn(iInitiator, iDestination);
+  }
 
   return TransmitKeypress(iInitiator, iDestination, CEC_USER_CONTROL_CODE_POWER) &&
     TransmitKeyRelease(iInitiator, iDestination);
